{#
/**
 * @file
 * An OPT-IN override, not a form-specific one: renders a submit as a real
 * `<button type="submit">` rather than core's `<input>` — so it agrees with
 * a `bb_theme:button` beside it, which is already a real `<button>`/`<a>`.
 * The create dialog's agreed grammar is one primary submit plus one ghost,
 * both buttons; before this override the row disagreed with itself, one
 * control an `<input>` and the other a `<button>`.
 *
 * REACHED BY NAME, BY WHOEVER WANTS IT. A form element states
 * `'#theme_wrappers' => ['input__submit__bb_button']` and Drupal's own `__`
 * suggestion ladder resolves it here, falling back to `input__submit` and
 * `input` for anything that does not. It was
 * `input--submit--bb-ticket-create.html.twig` — a Formdazzle FORM-ID rung
 * — until BB-420's branch review named that as a symptom: a template that
 * can only ever serve one form is a special case wearing a suggestion's
 * clothes, and the next form wanting the same button would have had to copy
 * it. `input--submit.html.twig`, the theme-wide override every other form's
 * `<input type="submit">` still renders through, is untouched: its rendering
 * is deliberate there.
 *
 * Drupal supplies the button's attributes, including its name, value and
 * disabled state. Only the tag and
 * the CLASS LIST change here — to `bb_theme:button`'s own primary-variant
 * classes, copied rather than composed through the component's own Twig
 * entry point, because that entry point prints its own `type` and `disabled`
 * attributes unconditionally and would duplicate the ones already in
 * `attributes`.
 *
 * THE LABEL IS `element['#value']`. Printing `attributes.value` would emit
 * an already-escaped attribute string as text, so a label that contains
 * `&` would read as `&amp;` to users and to the accessibility tree.
 *
 * @see web/themes/custom/bb_theme/templates/input--submit.html.twig
 * @see web/themes/custom/bb_theme/components/button/button.twig
 * @see web/core/themes/olivero/templates/form/input--submit--header-search.html.twig
 */
#}
{% set variant_classes = {
  'success': ['bg-state-running-ink', 'text-state-running-tint', 'border', 'border-transparent', 'hover:opacity-90'],
  'neutral': ['bg-surface', 'text-text', 'border', 'border-border', 'hover:bg-surface-2'],
  'primary': ['bg-primary', 'text-on-primary', 'border', 'border-transparent', 'hover:opacity-90'],
  'ghost': ['bg-transparent', 'text-text-light', 'border', 'border-transparent', 'hover:bg-surface-3', 'hover:text-text'],
  'danger': ['bg-transparent', 'text-state-unassigned-ink', 'border', 'border-state-unassigned', 'hover:bg-state-unassigned-tint'],
} %}
<button{{ attributes.addClass([
  'button', 'inline-flex', 'items-center', 'justify-center', 'gap-[6px]',
  'h-[30px]', 'px-[10px]', 'rounded-sm', 'text-caption', 'font-bold',
  'no-underline', 'cursor-pointer', 'disabled:opacity-60',
  'disabled:cursor-not-allowed',
]|merge(variant_classes[element['#bb_variant']|default('primary')]|default(variant_classes['primary']))) }}>{{ element['#value'] }}</button>{{ children }}
